      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not at all saying this is wrong...\nBut I\u0027m just not convinced it\u0027s right...\n\nAlthough I do think it is likely that the default buffer size is actually \u003e\u003d64kiB, however I believe that comes from a sysctl and thus cannot be guaranteed...\n\n---\n\nAlso note:\n    public static final int DEFAULT_RECV_BUFSIZE \u003d 8 * 1024;\n    public static final int SOCKET_RECV_BUFSIZE \u003d 64 * 1024;\n\njust because read buffer is limited to 8kb, it doesn\u0027t mean we don\u0027t need to buffer more than 1 packet if we read in a loop.  ie. a single send [dump request to kernel] could result in multiple messages needing to be read back.  so it needs to be deeply analyzed for each case.",
      "revId": "c5cfff7b2f4979d9fb429fb2b879da442ecc68a1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
