      "writtenOn": "2024-01-30T14:32:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Checked that on my cuttlefish instance, the NETLINK_ROUTE socket has a default buffer size of 114688(112k). Maybe Inet diag socket doesn\u0027t set the 64k buffer size as it\u0027s expecting a bigger default size? I added a definition of SOCKET_DUMP_RECV_BUFSIZE of 128k for socket in the getAndProcessNetlinkDumpMessages() function. Would this be enough? Or shall we set something even bigger?",
